{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792310649,"nonce":"YxTnJ1Q9EraAtPpjXcHBX4zGcwU=","title":"Map\u003cString,String\u003e.get() used directly inside a string concat prints the POINTER; assigning to a typed local first is correct. Cost me a ...","message":"**MINIMAL REPRO, 2026-08-18 at `884dfaf9`:**\n\n    var m = new Map\u003cString, String\u003e();\n    m.set(\"a\", \"hello\");\n    Sys.println(\"a=\" + m.get(\"a\"));        // a=46603240928   \u003c-- POINTER\n    var v:String = m.get(\"a\");\n    Sys.println(\"typed=\" + v);             // typed=hello     \u003c-- correct\n\n`haxe_stringmap_get` returns **raw u64 bits** by design (the mapping entry in\n`runtime_mapping.rs` says so: \"compiler casts back to resolved type parameter\nT\"). That cast happens on assignment to a typed local, but NOT when the call is\nan operand of a string concatenation — there the raw pointer is stringified as\nan integer.\n\n**WORKAROUND:** bind to a typed local before using the value.\n**Do not \"fix\" this by changing the runtime symbol** — the raw-u64 return is\nwhat makes value storage unboxed; the defect is the missing cast at the concat\nsite. Related: [[bugs_std_string_dynamic_unbox_and_erased_generics]],\n[[bugs_stringmap_null_get]].\n\n**IT PRODUCES CONVINCING FAKE DATA.** Eight distinct GGUF metadata values all\nprinted as ~3.0e10, decreasing by a uniform stride — which reads as \"the loader\nis returning addresses\" and sent me rewriting a working parser twice. **The\nwrite path was correct the whole time; only the DISPLAY was wrong.** When every\nvalue in a set looks like an address, suspect the read/print site before the\nproducer.\n\n**TWO OTHER ENUM-MATCH SHAPES THAT MISCOMPILE** (found while chasing this, on\n`GGUFReader.MetaValue`, an enum with 13 constructors):\n- `return switch (v) { case U8(x) | I8(x) | ...: Std.string(x); ... }` — garbage\n- the same match rewritten as `switch` with an early `return` per case —\n  **SIGILL (exit 132)**\n\n`readIntOr`'s shape — `switch` whose arms yield the payload directly into an\nInt-typed function return — is the one that works. Prefer it; do not convert a\nmulti-constructor payload to String inside the match.\n\n---\nArchived from Claude memory `bugs_map_string_get_returns_raw_pointer_in_concat` on 2026-10-18. A record of past work; open items in it may have their own issues.","files":null}]}